    {
      "id": "claim_f3cbc6938de84368af13e560a1237a39",
      "statement": "Deleting an OrgUser (delete_orguser_v1) runs in a transaction that first reassigns created_by on the org's Dashboard, Chart, Metric, KPI, ReportSnapshot and Alert rows to the acting admin and deletes the invitations the user issued; it refuses self-deletion and deleting a higher-level role. A new owned model must be added to that tuple to avoid orphaning.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/ddpui/core/orguserfunctions.py#L188-L219",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f18372ce0dd1e31c20eacf86e966e92c235e9ed918ac5871066b572db4bc0393:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5461e1bec091477fad8de3999bbe9dcc",
      "statement": "Org deletion is orchestrated by OrgCleanupService.delete_org (dry_run defaults to True) because external state must be removed first: Prefect deployments and blocks, the transformation layer (raising OrgCleanupServiceError if a dbt or git OrgTask is still used by an orchestrate pipeline), warehouse, Airbyte workspace, org users (UserPreferences deleted first; the Django User only if no other membership), the on-disk org directory, then OrgPlans, OrgPreferences and LlmSession rows whose DB constraints do not cascade, then KPIs before Metrics because of PROTECT, and finally the Org.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/ddpui/services/org_cleanup_service.py#L368-L399",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1416d3cc25eaf957a56db714eba17e374c87207c863e56a92b2aa99994c4d100:"
